  "source": {
    "title": "Warhammer 40,000: The App 2.7.0, data build 963, released 2026-09-30",
    "url": "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.gamesworkshop.w40k"
  },
  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "With **CHAOS KNIGHTS** as your [Army Faction](vsdata:core-rule/select-army-faction), your units with this ability get whichever [Dread abilities](vsdata:ability/chaos-knights.harbingers-of-dread) your army has active. **Deathly Terror (Aura)** is active as the battle begins.\n\nAs battle rounds 1, 3 and 5 begin, you can either:\n\n- pick another Dread ability that is not yet active\n- roll 2 D6 and make active the abilities, numbered 1-6 below, whose numbers they show\n\nOnce active, a Dread ability stays active for the rest of the battle. No Dread ability can be picked a second time, and a repeated result from the dice adds nothing. The Dread abilities are:\n\n- **Deathly Terror (Aura)**: enemy units up to 9\" from this model get -1 Ld.\n- **Despair (Aura)** (1): the same again, on top of **Deathly Terror (Aura)**.\n- **Doom** (2): this model's attacks against a **[battle-shocked](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock)** target get +1 to [Wound](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls).\n- **Darkness** (3): this model gets **[Stealth](vsdata:core-ability/stealth)**.\n- **Dismay (Aura)** (4): in [your opponent's Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase), at its [Battle-shock step](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock-step), every enemy unit under its **Starting Strength** up to 9\" from this model takes a [Battle-shock test](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock).\n- **Delirium (Aura)** (5): whenever an enemy unit up to 9\" from this model fails its Battle-shock test while **Below Half-strength**, that unit takes D3 [mortal wounds](vsdata:core-rule/mortal-wounds).\n- **Dominion** (6): Aura abilities of this model get +3\" range.",
